+</section>
diff --git a/src/content/announcements/-chaos-cubed-tiny-takeover.json b/src/content/announcements/-chaos-cubed-tiny-takeover.json
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9cd3d17
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/content/announcements/-chaos-cubed-tiny-takeover.json
@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+{
+  "id": "6a8385b9cc25977623a07bad",
+  "title": "🐢 Chaos Cubed / Tiny Takeover",
+  "author": "Jonathan Hill",
+  "topics": [
+    "miscellaneous",
+    "gameplay"
+  ],
+  "excerpt": "Hey everyone. The server is (finally!) updated to 26.2, which covers the Chaos Cubed and Tiny Takeover game drops. 🧊Chaos Cubed adds a new sulfur cave biome and their sulfur cube inhabitants who can be fed certain blocks to become…",
+  "date": "2026-08-17T17:12:23.842000-05:00",
+  "draft": false,
+  "body": "\n  \n  <p class=\"post-emphasis\">Hey everyone. The server is (finally!) updated to 26.2, which covers the Chaos Cubed and Tiny Takeover game drops.</p><ul><li><p><strong>🧊Chaos Cubed</strong> adds a new sulfur cave biome and their sulfur cube inhabitants who can be fed certain blocks to become different physics objects.</p></li><li><p><strong>🐥Tiny Takeover</strong> remodels all baby animals, makes name tags craftable, and adds the golden dandelion, which can keep mobs as babies forever!</p></li></ul><p>SSS has the following supporting and miscellaneous updates:</p><ul><li><p>🌎The resource world has been regenerated. Go find some sulfur caves!</p></li><li><p>🧊Sulfur cubes of the smallest size can drop a Sulfur Cube Head.</p></li><li><p>🎶The new Bounce music disc is playable in Walkman.</p></li><li><p>🏷️The server shop no longer buys name tags, as they are cheaply craftable.</p></li><li><p>😁Happy Ghasts you&#x27;ve protected (such as by naming them) can now be used with Impetus of Artemis.</p></li><li><p>💍Added /charm info to view info about a charm. This covers all charms, not just the Valor Shop ones.</p></li><li><p>🥔Poisonous potatoes can no longer be given to babies to prevent their growth. Use the golden dandelion!</p></li></ul><p>There were a ton of technical changes to the game behind the scenes for these updates, which contributed to the delays and required a number of updates from me to stabilize. If you notice anything behaving oddly (especially particles or in-game text from commands), please let me know.</p><p>Cheers! </p>\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"
+}
