+{
+  "id": "68af677730bc4e7fb221103e",
+  "title": "🍻 Tavern: Build Contest Winners",
+  "author": "Jonathan Hill",
+  "topics": [
+    "build-contest"
+  ],
+  "excerpt": "Hey @everyone. Time to announce the winners of the Tavern build contest! 🥇 1st Place : @NetworkGremlin and @gabreno! Your warp is set as `Tavern1`. 🥈 2nd Place : @J_, @Starmarsh, and @Daria! Your warp is set as `Mycobarrow`. 🥉 3rd Place :…",
+  "date": "2025-08-27T15:19:58.422000-05:00",
+  "draft": false,
+  "body": "\n  \n    \n  \n  <p>Hey @everyone. Time to announce the winners of the Tavern build contest!</p><ul><li><p>🥇<strong>1st Place</strong>: @NetworkGremlin and @gabreno! Your warp is set as `Tavern1`.</p></li><li><p>🥈 <strong>2nd Place</strong>: @J_, @Starmarsh, and @Daria! Your warp is set as `Mycobarrow`.</p></li><li><p>🥉 <strong>3rd Place</strong>: A tie!</p><ul><li><p>@J1mbers! Your warp is set as `DeadEnd`.</p></li><li><p>@Cubic and @nate! Your warp is set as `JourneysEnd`.</p></li></ul></li></ul><p>Thanks so much to all who submitted. Your prize bundles are in your ender chests, and lemme know if you want your warps renamed!</p><h2>🫶</h2>\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"
+}
diff --git a/src/content/announcements/1215-enchantment-changes.json b/src/content/announcements/1215-enchantment-changes.json
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3667839
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/content/announcements/1215-enchantment-changes.json
@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+{
+  "id": "67f61821ed0a7d387e8823d4",
+  "title": "📖1.21.5 Enchantment Changes",
+  "author": "Jonathan Hill",
+  "topics": [
+    "runecrafting"
+  ],
+  "excerpt": "Many Runecrafted enchantments have been reworked, updated, or removed. There are 5 new enchantments which we're revealing immediately ↓ There are 8 new curses which can be received from failed Runecrafts. These replace our previous 2…",
+  "date": "2025-04-12T14:31:00.120000-05:00",
+  "draft": false,
+  "body": "\n  \n  <h4>🔧System</h4><ul><li><p>Many Runecrafted enchantments have been reworked, updated, or removed.</p></li><li><p>There are 5 new <strong>enchantments</strong> which we&#x27;re revealing immediately ↓</p></li><li><p>There are 8 new <strong>curses</strong> which can be received from failed Runecrafts. These replace our previous 2 custom curses, and are mostly for fun, but some have potential use cases. These aren&#x27;t listed here, but they (and the two vanilla curses) are viewable in the Lexicon for reference.</p></li><li><p>Some enchantment recipes have been updated to more modern standards.</p></li></ul><h4>🎉New</h4><ul><li><p><strong>Ground Pound:</strong> </p><ul><li><p>Replaces Feather Falling V. Reduces fall damage and allows double sneaking while airborne to slam down and deal radial damage. Exclusive with Feather Falling &amp; Rocket Boosting.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Ragdoll: </strong></p><ul><li><p>Replaces Knockback III. Killing blows deals 3x knockback ignoring knockback resistance. Enemies hit by their body are stunned. Exclusive with Knockback.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Riposte:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Replaces Kinetic Battery. After a parry, your next attack automatically critically strikes.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Wire Cutters:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Port of Blast Protection V, which is reworked. Shears enchant which allows shearing explosive entities to “defuse” them. Exclusive with Mitosis &amp; Tithing.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Kaleidoscope:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Now a spyglass enchant instead of a charm.</p></li></ul></li></ul><h4>✨Reworked</h4><ul><li><p>All Chestplate &quot;Aspects&quot; have been renamed to “Avatars”, e.g. “Aspect of the Shulker” is now “Avatar of Shulkers”. This differentiates them from the DoT Aspects, and subjectively we feel it sounds cooler.</p></li></ul><ul><li><p><strong>Battering Ram:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Bash (double block) to rapidly dash forward, pushing and stunning enemies you collide with.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Blast Protection:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Defuse mechanic replaced with an Absorption “blast shield” upon taking blast damage, granting knockback immunity and damage reduction while it holds.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Executioner:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Now a 1-level Looting mutual. Executes below 5% health and grants +200% head drop rates.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Fencing:</strong></p><ul><li><p>After attacking, you can double-tap a movement key to hop invulnerably in that direction.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Frost Walker</strong>: </p><ul><li><p>Removed Runecrafted level III. Innately buffed to grant bonus speed on ice and snow blocks and convert powder snow to regular snow.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Hot Rod:</strong></p><ul><li><p><em>Sears</em> some caught fish, doubling their restored hunger and sell price, and allows lava fishing for 2x <em>sear</em> chance.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Paradigm of Lust</strong>: </p><ul><li><p>Enemies targeting a spouse are <em>scorned</em>, allowing you to leap strike them from afar, <strong><em>but</em></strong> if a spouse dies in combat, you wither away unless you enact reckless vengeance against their killer.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Paradigm of Greed</strong>: </p><ul><li><p>You can form lifelong <em>contracts</em> with humanoid mobs using raw gold, <strong><em>but</em></strong> if ever you don&#x27;t re-up a contractor, they <em>betray</em> you.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Paradigm of Sloth:</strong></p><ul><li><p>You can <em>lumber</em>, moving slower and gaining slow, massive attacks, <strong><em>but</em></strong> lumbering replaces sprinting.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Shockwave:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Renamed to <strong>Undertow</strong>. Now releases a radial wave from you which pushes away enemies.</p></li></ul><p><strong>Singularity:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Renamed to <strong>Snare</strong>. Now releases ropes which pull enemies towards the impact point.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Skewering</strong>: </p><ul><li><p>Attacks gain range and <em>pierce</em> in a 3-prong cone, and throws bypass shields and <em>pierce</em> enemies. <em>Pierced</em> enemies are slowed.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Utility Belt:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Grants leggings a <em>belt</em>, a 9-slot item inventory. Shift right clicking them swaps the contents of their belt and your hotbar.</p></li></ul></li></ul><h4>📝Adjusted</h4><p class=\"post-small\">All changes are relative to current mechanics; unlisted = unchanged. Any very minor adjustments also unlisted. Use the Lexicon if you want every detail! ➕Buff, 🟰Neutral, ➖Nerf</p><ul><li><p>➕<strong>Avatar of Bees: </strong></p><ul><li><p>Grants +1 block reach and prevents bees from targeting you.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➕<strong>Avatar of Ender Dragons:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Fires a dragon fireball instead of continuous dragon breath.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➕<strong>Avatar of Iron Golems:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Grants +2❤️ max health instead of bonus knockback.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➕<strong>Avatar of Shulkers:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Shell mode is now activated by sneak punching below you, grants knockback immunity, and only converts arrows to Shulker bullets.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➕<strong>Avatar of Slimes:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Replaced random slimes on damage with a <strong>split</strong> at 75%, 50%, and 25% health, spawning a slime which draws aggro.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➕<strong>Bane of Arthropods</strong>: </p><ul><li><p>Always slows for the full duration (yes, it slows) and works against Shulkers (not new, but stating for visibility).</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➕<strong>Blitz:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Max level reduced, III → II. Same strength at max level.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➕<strong>Bottom Feeder:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Pulls from a new <strong>scrap table</strong> with grab bag-style items.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➖<strong>Bounty Hunter:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Only rolls to spawn a bounty on-kill. Reduces AFK silver collecting, though can result in more bounties during active gameplay.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➖<strong>Chaining:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Nerfed chain range, 16 blocks → 12.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➕<strong>Eldritch Inclination:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Luck gained from void damage now stacks. Now causes Wardens to warn you 1 additional time before they spawn.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➖<strong>Extinction:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Can stack against any non-player entity. Damage against non-bosses capped to 5-10 ❤. Rune locale mobs now treated as unique entity types.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➕<strong>Fire Aspect:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Cuts healing of burning targets by 50%.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➕<strong>Flare:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Entities hit directly glow for 30 seconds.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➕<strong>Green Thumb:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Max level reduced, III → II. Same strength at max level.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➖<strong>Howling:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Attack speed per stack reduced, 10% → 5%. Offhand howl damage reduced, 37.5% → 25%.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➕<strong>Multishot:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Note that this enchant is buffed by projectiles bypassing iframes.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➕<strong>Paradigm of Vainglory:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Replaced <em>cowering</em> slow with +10% speed to reduce reliance on mobility/Envy. The key punishment is intended to be exiting combat, not the debuff.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➖<strong>Pestilence &amp; Plague Aspect:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Spread is now delayed and only to the 1-3 closest enemies in range.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➕<strong>Riptide:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Now plays well with most enchants, and so is now only exclusive with Loyalty.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➕<strong>Rocket Boosting:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Max level reduced, III → II. Same strength at max level.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➖<strong>Schrödinger’s Thumb:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Max level increased, I → II. Same strength at max level.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➖<strong>Slingshot</strong>: </p><ul><li><p>Can no longer store equipment.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➕<strong>Soul Speed:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Removed durability drain.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➕<strong>Sundering</strong>: </p><ul><li><p>Now deals +1❤ attack damage, and stacks 3 times for 4❤ instead of 5 times for 3❤.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➕<strong>Sweeping Edge</strong>: Sweeps even when no target is hit directly.</p></li></ul><h4><strong>❌</strong><strong>Removed</strong></h4><ul><li><p><strong>Aspect of the Blaze</strong>: </p><ul><li><p>Struggled to find a good home since losing Blaze pacifying, which we don&#x27;t plan to readd.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Crucifying</strong>: </p><ul><li><p>Doesn&#x27;t see much use, nor is it worth the space.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Feather Falling V</strong>: </p><ul><li><p>Replaced by <strong>Ground Pound</strong>, see above.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Frost Walker III</strong>: </p><ul><li><p>Lava walking is better served by Striders. Vanilla enchant is now innately buffed, see above.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Haunted Bulwark</strong>: </p><ul><li><p>Doesn&#x27;t see much use or fit our modern ideals for shields.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Knockback III</strong>: </p><ul><li><p>Replaced by <strong>Ragdoll</strong>, see above.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Lightning Rod</strong>: </p><ul><li><p>Doesn&#x27;t see much use or fit our modern ideals for shields.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Misanthropy</strong>: </p><ul><li><p>Unnecessary now that Extinction works against any target.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Phantom Strike</strong>: </p><ul><li><p>We&#x27;re not fond of single-target DPS enchants competing with AoE ones.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Point Blank</strong>: </p><ul><li><p>Fills an odd space as a bow enchant. Now better serviced by options like Valor <strong>Cerberus</strong>.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Rune Scented</strong>: </p><ul><li><p>Replaced by the Valor <strong>Mark of the Cult</strong>.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Sapiovore</strong>: </p><ul><li><p>Replaced by the Valor <strong>R.E.D.</strong> armor.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Shadow Shot</strong>: </p><ul><li><p>We&#x27;re not fond of single-target DPS enchants competing with AoE ones.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Swift Sneak IV</strong>: </p><ul><li><p>Largely replaced by the Valor <strong>Umbral</strong> armor.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Overload</strong>: </p><ul><li><p>Plagued by balance issues, only used in abuse cases.</p></li></ul></li></ul>\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"
+}
diff --git a/src/content/announcements/1215-gameplay-changes.json b/src/content/announcements/1215-gameplay-changes.json
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..b905246
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/content/announcements/1215-gameplay-changes.json
@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+{
+  "id": "67f7701822b7236bc1c2de89",
+  "title": "⛏️1.21.5 Gameplay Changes",
+  "author": "Jonathan Hill",
+  "topics": [
+    "gameplay",
+    "miscellaneous"
+  ],
+  "excerpt": "The Great Runic Shift has fully transformed the following locales: 💨Gusts: New locale - Aethryn, the Helm of Terados . Floating islands holding an old observatory. Once used for navigation, now only the Breezes call it home. 💎Stones: New…",
+  "date": "2025-04-12T14:29:00.024000-05:00",
+  "draft": false,
+  "body": "\n  \n  <h4>🪄Rune Locales</h4><p>The Great Runic Shift has fully transformed the following locales:</p><ul><li><p><strong>💨Gusts: </strong>New locale - <strong>Aethryn, the Helm of Terados</strong>. Floating islands holding an old observatory. Once used for navigation, now only the Breezes call it home.</p></li><li><p><strong>💎Stones:</strong> New locale - <strong>Ruit, the Shimmering Grotto</strong>. A cave of geodes beneath a giant tree, with magical waters that empower the Silverfish within.</p></li><li><p><strong>🐝Vitality:</strong> New locale - <strong>Thriaechor, the Amber Eaves</strong>. The bees in this canopy of the great tree above Ruit do not take kindly to visitors!</p></li></ul><p>The following locales are also affected by the Runic Shift:</p><ul><li><p><strong>❄️Chills:</strong> Now housed in <strong>Skatheim, the Winter Bastion</strong> (previously the Mortus locale).</p></li><li><p><strong>🔥Cinders:</strong> Now home to Blazes instead of Wither Skeletons.</p></li><li><p><strong>💀Mortus:</strong> Now housed in <strong>Arkose, the Crimson Crypt</strong> (previously the Stones locale).</p></li></ul><p>Additionally, the following changes are applied to all locales:</p><ul><li><p>The base rune drop rate is increased from 3% to 5%.</p></li><li><p>The most difficult and frustrating locales have been toned down - lower stats, shorter levitation from Kuiper shulkers, and no Thorns on the Mystic Grove witches.</p></li><li><p>In exchange for the above, some locales have more spawners to make them harder to cheese. </p><ul><li><p>Also note the Extinction changes in the Enchantments changelog, which reduces the ease of farming runes late game.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>We hope this combines to make farming runes more enjoyable and less polarizing.</p></li></ul><h4>✨Luck</h4><p>Now affects many areas of gameplay:</p><ul><li><p>Increases the odds of high-value rolls from Bottom Feeder, Schrödinger’s Thumb, the boardwalk claw machine, and the Tip Jar charm.</p></li><li><p>Increases the activation odds of Hot Rod, Hands-On Learning, the Juniper Sprig charm, and the Runic Compass charm.</p></li><li><p>Increases the average drop count from Trawling, Tithing, Cultist bosses, and the Opulence Runic Tome spell.</p></li><li><p>Increases the chance of Rune and Gem drops in survival worlds and duping the Shiny Gold Coin.</p></li><li><p>Reduces the odds of hostile mob heads during whack-a-staff.</p></li><li><p>Increases the drop rate of heads. (This isn’t new, but stating it for visibility)</p></li><li><p>Increases the quality of fishing loot. (This is vanilla, but stating it for visibility)</p></li></ul><h4>💎Socketing</h4><ul><li><p>A new <strong>Gem of Favor</strong> has been added, granting +0.25 Luck per gem. These can be obtained in the same way as all standard stat gems.</p></li><li><p>Armor now only has 4 sockets. Gems are not buffed to compensate - this is an intentional nerf to give room for power in more interesting areas.</p></li></ul><h4>🔱Tridents</h4><ul><li><p>Can now be crafted using 3 Twinkling Sea Crystals, 1 Nautilus Shell, and 1 Prismarine Shard.</p></li><li><p>Riptide is now more compatible with other trident enchants, including Runecrafted ones, and so is now only exclusive with Loyalty.</p></li><li><p>Note that Loyalty tridents are already buffed to return if they fall into the void and generally return faster.</p></li></ul><h4>🛡️Shields</h4><ul><li><p>Shields can now <strong>parry</strong> by blocking &lt;=0.3 seconds before a strike. Parrying an attack stuns the attacker, while parrying a projectile reflects it.</p></li><li><p>Shields can now <strong>bash</strong> by quickly double blocking, pushes enemies away in a radius in front of you.</p></li><li><p>Axe attacks now only disable shields for 1.6 seconds rather than 5.</p></li><li><p>We intend these changes to make shields more considerable as a primary accessory into the late game.</p></li></ul><h4>📝Miscellaneous</h4><ul><li><p>Applying splash or lingering potions to targets other than yourself now grants mcMMO Alchemy experience.</p></li><li><p>Projectiles now bypass invulnerability frames.</p></li><li><p><strong>Stuns</strong> are a more present mechanic from various items and enchants. Stuns prevent the target from acting, but are broken if they take direct damage.</p></li></ul>\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"
+}
diff --git a/src/content/announcements/1215-heirloom-faq.json b/src/content/announcements/1215-heirloom-faq.json
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..7f6387c
--- /dev/null
