@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+{
+  "id": "681fc6b9c26383378abc9593",
+  "title": "📖1.21.5 Runecrafting Expansion",
+  "author": "Jonathan Hill",
+  "topics": [
+    "runecrafting"
+  ],
+  "excerpt": "Hello researchers! Thanks for joining today's research expeditions. We've discovered so much already, but this is just the beginning! I'm here to give you a quick summary of what was discovered, and how research and enchant discoveries…",
+  "date": "2025-05-10T16:48:57.080000-05:00",
+  "draft": false,
+  "body": "\n  \n  <h4><strong>📖Runecrafting Expansion: Research Overview</strong></h4><p>Hello researchers! Thanks for joining today&#x27;s research expeditions. We&#x27;ve discovered so much already, but this is just the beginning! I&#x27;m here to give you a quick summary of what was discovered, and how research and enchant discoveries will work throughout this event.</p><p class=\"post-emphasis\"><strong>📝Event Summary</strong></p><ul><li><p>Together, we discovered two new rune locales:</p><ul><li><p>🌆<strong>Val, the Ancient Capital</strong>, home of the <strong>Rune of Echoes</strong>, representing <em>sound</em> and <em>repetition</em>.</p></li><li><p>🌩️<strong>Enelysios, the Deadly Current</strong>, home of the <strong>Rune of Sparks</strong>, representing <em>electricity</em> and <em>inspiration</em>.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>Upon discovering Enelysios, the nascent locale <strong>surged with energy</strong>, spawning an <strong>apex enemy</strong>.</p></li><li><p>The apex enemy dropped <strong>Boundary Fragments</strong>, which we used to uncover information about 8 new enchants.</p></li></ul><p class=\"post-emphasis\"><strong>🔬Research Mechanics</strong></p><ul><li><p>⬆️The Arcanum has been upgraded, but at a cost:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Discovering new enchants now requires perfectly accurate recipes</strong> - runes must be submitted in perfect order.</p></li><li><p>The Arcanum now salvages 2 runes from failed runecrafts. If you <em>nearly</em> discover an <strong>active research project</strong> by using its <strong>correct runes in the wrong order</strong>, The Arcanum detects this, notifies you, and salvages 4 runes.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>🔋A random locale <strong>surges with energy</strong> 4 times daily, at 10:00 AM, 2:00 PM, 6:00 PM, and 10:00 PM CDT:</p><ul><li><p>The surging locale spawns a boundary-touched <strong>apex</strong> boss and starts <strong>overcharging</strong>, accelerated by player deaths and slowed by damaging the apex.</p></li><li><p>The apex periodically spawns damageable <strong>runic tears</strong> and releases <strong>diffusion waves</strong> from them and itself, dealing damage which bypasses most enchants.</p></li><li><p>If slain, the apex drops <strong>1 Boundary Fragment</strong>. If the locale fully overcharges, the surge ends unsuccessfully.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>📑Active projects roll a new <strong>research quest</strong> daily at the start of the hour of their discovery.</p><ul><li><p>Research quests use shared progress - once anyone completes it, that project&#x27;s quest is done for the day. Work together to complete each quest daily!</p></li><li><p>Projects can be viewed using /lexicon project &lt;project number&gt;.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>🧭A <strong>quest board</strong> has been set up on the back wall of /warp ArcanumResearchLab:</p><ul><li><p>Active projects have a board entry that can be interacted with to progress their quest (if applicable) or submit a <strong>Boundary Fragment</strong> to it.</p></li><li><p>Completing a project&#x27;s quest grants it <strong>+10%</strong> Research Progress. Submitting a Boundary Fragment directly to a project grants it <strong>+50%</strong> Research Progress.</p></li><li><p>When a project hits 100% progress, new information about it is discovered, up to <strong>4 times</strong> per project.</p></li><li><p>Alternatively, a Boundary Fragment can be <strong>submitted directly to the Arcanum</strong> to scry for new enchants - this will randomly either uncover information about a new enchantment, beginning its research project, or add 50% progress to an ongoing project.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>🧑‍🎓Once an enchant is discovered, its <strong>top researcher</strong> (whoever contributed the most research progress to it) will be contributed as an additional discoverer!</p></li></ul><p>Thanks everyone for your help today. There are over <strong>50 new enchants to discover</strong>. Feel free to ask any questions in ⁠<a href=\"https://discord.gg/tXtcqMwFaM\">📖arcanum-expansion</a>. Good luck and happy researching!</p>\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"
+}
