+{
+  "id": "68ce14020cf3be416cc62679",
+  "title": "📝Build Contest Winners &amp; Spooky Springs Poll",
+  "author": "Jonathan Hill",
+  "topics": [
+    "build-contest"
+  ],
+  "excerpt": "Hey @everyone. We're here to announce the winners of the Forge build contest, and to poll you all in prep for Halloween festivities next month! 🔨 Forge Contest Winners 🥇 1st Place : A tie! @projectrallus, @PenroseParadox, and @Bobola0!…",
+  "date": "2025-09-19T21:46:26.850000-05:00",
+  "draft": false,
+  "body": "\n  \n    \n  \n  <p>Hey @everyone. We&#x27;re here to announce the winners of the Forge build contest, and to poll you all in prep for Halloween festivities next month!</p><h4>🔨<strong>Forge Contest Winners</strong></h4><ul><li><p>🥇<strong>1st Place</strong>: A tie!</p></li><li><p>@projectrallus, @PenroseParadox, and @Bobola0! Your warp is set as `Pigforge`, as requested.</p></li><li><p>@rillabel and Stolas_Owl! Your warp is set as `VulcanForge`.</p></li><li><p>🥉 <strong>3rd Place</strong>: @Maidl, @TroyTheCrafter, @Hollow, and @jpguitar27! Your warp is set as `Forge3`</p></li></ul><p>Thanks to all who submitted. Your prize bundles are in your ender chests, or in your inventory if they couldn&#x27;t fit, and let us know if you want your warps renamed!</p><h4>🎃Spooky Springs Poll</h4><p>For the uninitiated, Spooky Springs is a special build contest we sometimes run near Halloween where each group builds in separate plots in a shared Halloween town. This gives you limited space to work with, but everyone gets to build near each other. To see some examples, check the `SpookySprings2017`, `SpookySprings2019`, and `SpookySprings2023` warps.</p><p>This year, we&#x27;d like to gauge what you&#x27;re all most interested in: the typical plot-based format, a more classic build contest in the survival world, or something else. Use the poll <a href=\"https://discord.com/channels/97121264988082176/329404551528579075/1418695973135319052\">here</a> and share any additional feedback <a href=\"https://discord.com/channels/97121264988082176/138080509577134081\">here</a>. Thanks!</p><h2>🫶</h2>\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"
+}
