@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+{
+  "id": "6850ab535b7789422dfb6e2f",
+  "title": "⚔️Contest Reminder, PvP Tournament, Paragons",
+  "author": "Jonathan Hill",
+  "topics": [
+    "build-contest",
+    "event"
+  ],
+  "excerpt": "Hey again everyone, hope you're well. We've got reminders and news about upcoming events and this map's awarded Paragons being distributed.",
+  "date": "2025-06-16T18:48:11.978000-05:00",
+  "draft": false,
+  "body": "\n  \n  <p class=\"post-emphasis\">Hey again everyone, hope you&#x27;re well. We&#x27;ve got reminders and news about upcoming events and this map&#x27;s awarded Paragons being distributed.</p><h4>🪔<strong>Build Contest Reminder</strong></h4><p>Quick reminder that your build contest entries are due in less than 24 hours - submit them by Sunday, June 15, 2025 11:59 PM PST for them to be judged!</p><h4>⚔️<strong>BYOG PvP Tournament</strong></h4><p>We&#x27;re holding a “bring your own gear” PvP tournament next weekend, hosted by MrJoned . This event is also visible on our <a href=\"/calendar/\">calendar</a>. Most new content of course hasn&#x27;t had much PvP testing, so we expect this to be a bit wacky. We&#x27;ll aim to do a balance pass on some outliers this week, but please be pragmatic and just try to have fun!</p><ul><li><p> Tournament Date: Saturday, June 21, 2025 1:00 PM</p></li><li><p>Prizes: TBD</p></li></ul><h4>✨<strong>Paragons</strong></h4><p>Starmarsh™ and ElectricSparx have officially received their <strong>Paragons</strong>, which I&#x27;m formally announcing here in an effort for the Paragons to be more well-known. These are unique items designed in partnership with each of them, though as usual with Paragons there&#x27;s a possibility that a subdued version of one or both of these becomes generally available in the future (that&#x27;s where the Runic Tome came from!)</p><ul><li><p>Following a spark of inspiration, @Starmarsh™ has engineered <strong>CoSMOS</strong>, a marvelous rebreather which can alchemically empower the wearer, mutating their physiology or injecting potions from provided reagents.,</p></li><li><p>From deep within the Arcanum&#x27;s now-corrupted lower shelves, @ElectricSparx has discovered the <strong>Eldritch Codex</strong>, a Runic Grimoire whose arcane script has been altered by the void, now casting an entirely alternate set of corrupted spells.</p></li><li><p>We&#x27;ll soon add a ‘/paragon’ command to view the existing Paragons in-game, for those curious.,</p></li></ul><p>There have been other updates and bug fixes this week, though none worth taking up announcement space, and the other new content announced recently is still planned and underway. Thanks for your time and good luck completing your Shrine builds. ✌️</p>\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"
+}
