diff --git a/src/content/posts/1215-enchantment-changes.html b/src/content/posts/1215-enchantment-changes.html
deleted file mode 100644
index 702b158..0000000
--- a/src/content/posts/1215-enchantment-changes.html
+++ /dev/null
@@ -1,15 +0,0 @@
-
-  
-  <h4>🔧System</h4><ul><li><p>Many Runecrafted enchantments have been reworked, updated, or removed.</p></li><li><p>There are 5 new <strong>enchantments</strong> which we&#x27;re revealing immediately ↓</p></li><li><p>There are 8 new <strong>curses</strong> which can be received from failed Runecrafts. These replace our previous 2 custom curses, and are mostly for fun, but some have potential use cases. These aren&#x27;t listed here, but they (and the two vanilla curses) are viewable in the Lexicon for reference.</p></li><li><p>Some enchantment recipes have been updated to more modern standards.</p></li></ul><h4>🎉New</h4><ul><li><p><strong>Ground Pound:</strong> </p><ul><li><p>Replaces Feather Falling V. Reduces fall damage and allows double sneaking while airborne to slam down and deal radial damage. Exclusive with Feather Falling &amp; Rocket Boosting.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Ragdoll: </strong></p><ul><li><p>Replaces Knockback III. Killing blows deals 3x knockback ignoring knockback resistance. Enemies hit by their body are stunned. Exclusive with Knockback.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Riposte:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Replaces Kinetic Battery. After a parry, your next attack automatically critically strikes.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Wire Cutters:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Port of Blast Protection V, which is reworked. Shears enchant which allows shearing explosive entities to “defuse” them. Exclusive with Mitosis &amp; Tithing.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Kaleidoscope:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Now a spyglass enchant instead of a charm.</p></li></ul></li></ul><h4>✨Reworked</h4><ul><li><p>All Chestplate &quot;Aspects&quot; have been renamed to “Avatars”, e.g. “Aspect of the Shulker” is now “Avatar of Shulkers”. This differentiates them from the DoT Aspects, and subjectively we feel it sounds cooler.</p></li></ul><ul><li><p><strong>Battering Ram:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Bash (double block) to rapidly dash forward, pushing and stunning enemies you collide with.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Blast Protection:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Defuse mechanic replaced with an Absorption “blast shield” upon taking blast damage, granting knockback immunity and damage reduction while it holds.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Executioner:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Now a 1-level Looting mutual. Executes below 5% health and grants +200% head drop rates.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Fencing:</strong></p><ul><li><p>After attacking, you can double-tap a movement key to hop invulnerably in that direction.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Frost Walker</strong>: </p><ul><li><p>Removed Runecrafted level III. Innately buffed to grant bonus speed on ice and snow blocks and convert powder snow to regular snow.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Hot Rod:</strong></p><ul><li><p><em>Sears</em> some caught fish, doubling their restored hunger and sell price, and allows lava fishing for 2x <em>sear</em> chance.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Paradigm of Lust</strong>: </p><ul><li><p>Enemies targeting a spouse are <em>scorned</em>, allowing you to leap strike them from afar, <strong><em>but</em></strong> if a spouse dies in combat, you wither away unless you enact reckless vengeance against their killer.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Paradigm of Greed</strong>: </p><ul><li><p>You can form lifelong <em>contracts</em> with humanoid mobs using raw gold, <strong><em>but</em></strong> if ever you don&#x27;t re-up a contractor, they <em>betray</em> you.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Paradigm of Sloth:</strong></p><ul><li><p>You can <em>lumber</em>, moving slower and gaining slow, massive attacks, <strong><em>but</em></strong> lumbering replaces sprinting.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Shockwave:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Renamed to <strong>Undertow</strong>. Now releases a radial wave from you which pushes away enemies.</p></li></ul><p><strong>Singularity:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Renamed to <strong>Snare</strong>. Now releases ropes which pull enemies towards the impact point.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Skewering</strong>: </p><ul><li><p>Attacks gain range and <em>pierce</em> in a 3-prong cone, and throws bypass shields and <em>pierce</em> enemies. <em>Pierced</em> enemies are slowed.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Utility Belt:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Grants leggings a <em>belt</em>, a 9-slot item inventory. Shift right clicking them swaps the contents of their belt and your hotbar.</p></li></ul></li></ul><h4>📝Adjusted</h4><p class="post-small">All changes are relative to current mechanics; unlisted = unchanged. Any very minor adjustments also unlisted. Use the Lexicon if you want every detail! ➕Buff, 🟰Neutral, ➖Nerf</p><ul><li><p>➕<strong>Avatar of Bees: </strong></p><ul><li><p>Grants +1 block reach and prevents bees from targeting you.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➕<strong>Avatar of Ender Dragons:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Fires a dragon fireball instead of continuous dragon breath.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➕<strong>Avatar of Iron Golems:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Grants +2❤️ max health instead of bonus knockback.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➕<strong>Avatar of Shulkers:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Shell mode is now activated by sneak punching below you, grants knockback immunity, and only converts arrows to Shulker bullets.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➕<strong>Avatar of Slimes:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Replaced random slimes on damage with a <strong>split</strong> at 75%, 50%, and 25% health, spawning a slime which draws aggro.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➕<strong>Bane of Arthropods</strong>: </p><ul><li><p>Always slows for the full duration (yes, it slows) and works against Shulkers (not new, but stating for visibility).</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➕<strong>Blitz:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Max level reduced, III → II. Same strength at max level.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➕<strong>Bottom Feeder:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Pulls from a new <strong>scrap table</strong> with grab bag-style items.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➖<strong>Bounty Hunter:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Only rolls to spawn a bounty on-kill. Reduces AFK silver collecting, though can result in more bounties during active gameplay.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➖<strong>Chaining:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Nerfed chain range, 16 blocks → 12.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➕<strong>Eldritch Inclination:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Luck gained from void damage now stacks. Now causes Wardens to warn you 1 additional time before they spawn.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➖<strong>Extinction:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Can stack against any non-player entity. Damage against non-bosses capped to 5-10 ❤. Rune locale mobs now treated as unique entity types.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➕<strong>Fire Aspect:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Cuts healing of burning targets by 50%.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➕<strong>Flare:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Entities hit directly glow for 30 seconds.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➕<strong>Green Thumb:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Max level reduced, III → II. Same strength at max level.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➖<strong>Howling:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Attack speed per stack reduced, 10% → 5%. Offhand howl damage reduced, 37.5% → 25%.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➕<strong>Multishot:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Note that this enchant is buffed by projectiles bypassing iframes.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➕<strong>Paradigm of Vainglory:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Replaced <em>cowering</em> slow with +10% speed to reduce reliance on mobility/Envy. The key punishment is intended to be exiting combat, not the debuff.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➖<strong>Pestilence &amp; Plague Aspect:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Spread is now delayed and only to the 1-3 closest enemies in range.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➕<strong>Riptide:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Now plays well with most enchants, and so is now only exclusive with Loyalty.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➕<strong>Rocket Boosting:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Max level reduced, III → II. Same strength at max level.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➖<strong>Schrödinger’s Thumb:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Max level increased, I → II. Same strength at max level.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➖<strong>Slingshot</strong>: </p><ul><li><p>Can no longer store equipment.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➕<strong>Soul Speed:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Removed durability drain.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➕<strong>Sundering</strong>: </p><ul><li><p>Now deals +1❤ attack damage, and stacks 3 times for 4❤ instead of 5 times for 3❤.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>➕<strong>Sweeping Edge</strong>: Sweeps even when no target is hit directly.</p></li></ul><h4><strong>❌</strong><strong>Removed</strong></h4><ul><li><p><strong>Aspect of the Blaze</strong>: </p><ul><li><p>Struggled to find a good home since losing Blaze pacifying, which we don&#x27;t plan to readd.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Crucifying</strong>: </p><ul><li><p>Doesn&#x27;t see much use, nor is it worth the space.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Feather Falling V</strong>: </p><ul><li><p>Replaced by <strong>Ground Pound</strong>, see above.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Frost Walker III</strong>: </p><ul><li><p>Lava walking is better served by Striders. Vanilla enchant is now innately buffed, see above.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Haunted Bulwark</strong>: </p><ul><li><p>Doesn&#x27;t see much use or fit our modern ideals for shields.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Knockback III</strong>: </p><ul><li><p>Replaced by <strong>Ragdoll</strong>, see above.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Lightning Rod</strong>: </p><ul><li><p>Doesn&#x27;t see much use or fit our modern ideals for shields.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Misanthropy</strong>: </p><ul><li><p>Unnecessary now that Extinction works against any target.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Phantom Strike</strong>: </p><ul><li><p>We&#x27;re not fond of single-target DPS enchants competing with AoE ones.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Point Blank</strong>: </p><ul><li><p>Fills an odd space as a bow enchant. Now better serviced by options like Valor <strong>Cerberus</strong>.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Rune Scented</strong>: </p><ul><li><p>Replaced by the Valor <strong>Mark of the Cult</strong>.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Sapiovore</strong>: </p><ul><li><p>Replaced by the Valor <strong>R.E.D.</strong> armor.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Shadow Shot</strong>: </p><ul><li><p>We&#x27;re not fond of single-target DPS enchants competing with AoE ones.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Swift Sneak IV</strong>: </p><ul><li><p>Largely replaced by the Valor <strong>Umbral</strong> armor.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Overload</strong>: </p><ul><li><p>Plagued by balance issues, only used in abuse cases.</p></li></ul></li></ul>
-
