@@ -1,15 +0,0 @@
-
-  
-  <h4>🪄Rune Locales</h4><p>The Great Runic Shift has fully transformed the following locales:</p><ul><li><p><strong>💨Gusts: </strong>New locale - <strong>Aethryn, the Helm of Terados</strong>. Floating islands holding an old observatory. Once used for navigation, now only the Breezes call it home.</p></li><li><p><strong>💎Stones:</strong> New locale - <strong>Ruit, the Shimmering Grotto</strong>. A cave of geodes beneath a giant tree, with magical waters that empower the Silverfish within.</p></li><li><p><strong>🐝Vitality:</strong> New locale - <strong>Thriaechor, the Amber Eaves</strong>. The bees in this canopy of the great tree above Ruit do not take kindly to visitors!</p></li></ul><p>The following locales are also affected by the Runic Shift:</p><ul><li><p><strong>❄️Chills:</strong> Now housed in <strong>Skatheim, the Winter Bastion</strong> (previously the Mortus locale).</p></li><li><p><strong>🔥Cinders:</strong> Now home to Blazes instead of Wither Skeletons.</p></li><li><p><strong>💀Mortus:</strong> Now housed in <strong>Arkose, the Crimson Crypt</strong> (previously the Stones locale).</p></li></ul><p>Additionally, the following changes are applied to all locales:</p><ul><li><p>The base rune drop rate is increased from 3% to 5%.</p></li><li><p>The most difficult and frustrating locales have been toned down - lower stats, shorter levitation from Kuiper shulkers, and no Thorns on the Mystic Grove witches.</p></li><li><p>In exchange for the above, some locales have more spawners to make them harder to cheese. </p><ul><li><p>Also note the Extinction changes in the Enchantments changelog, which reduces the ease of farming runes late game.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>We hope this combines to make farming runes more enjoyable and less polarizing.</p></li></ul><h4>✨Luck</h4><p>Now affects many areas of gameplay:</p><ul><li><p>Increases the odds of high-value rolls from Bottom Feeder, Schrödinger’s Thumb, the boardwalk claw machine, and the Tip Jar charm.</p></li><li><p>Increases the activation odds of Hot Rod, Hands-On Learning, the Juniper Sprig charm, and the Runic Compass charm.</p></li><li><p>Increases the average drop count from Trawling, Tithing, Cultist bosses, and the Opulence Runic Tome spell.</p></li><li><p>Increases the chance of Rune and Gem drops in survival worlds and duping the Shiny Gold Coin.</p></li><li><p>Reduces the odds of hostile mob heads during whack-a-staff.</p></li><li><p>Increases the drop rate of heads. (This isn’t new, but stating it for visibility)</p></li><li><p>Increases the quality of fishing loot. (This is vanilla, but stating it for visibility)</p></li></ul><h4>💎Socketing</h4><ul><li><p>A new <strong>Gem of Favor</strong> has been added, granting +0.25 Luck per gem. These can be obtained in the same way as all standard stat gems.</p></li><li><p>Armor now only has 4 sockets. Gems are not buffed to compensate - this is an intentional nerf to give room for power in more interesting areas.</p></li></ul><h4>🔱Tridents</h4><ul><li><p>Can now be crafted using 3 Twinkling Sea Crystals, 1 Nautilus Shell, and 1 Prismarine Shard.</p></li><li><p>Riptide is now more compatible with other trident enchants, including Runecrafted ones, and so is now only exclusive with Loyalty.</p></li><li><p>Note that Loyalty tridents are already buffed to return if they fall into the void and generally return faster.</p></li></ul><h4>🛡️Shields</h4><ul><li><p>Shields can now <strong>parry</strong> by blocking &lt;=0.3 seconds before a strike. Parrying an attack stuns the attacker, while parrying a projectile reflects it.</p></li><li><p>Shields can now <strong>bash</strong> by quickly double blocking, pushes enemies away in a radius in front of you.</p></li><li><p>Axe attacks now only disable shields for 1.6 seconds rather than 5.</p></li><li><p>We intend these changes to make shields more considerable as a primary accessory into the late game.</p></li></ul><h4>📝Miscellaneous</h4><ul><li><p>Applying splash or lingering potions to targets other than yourself now grants mcMMO Alchemy experience.</p></li><li><p>Projectiles now bypass invulnerability frames.</p></li><li><p><strong>Stuns</strong> are a more present mechanic from various items and enchants. Stuns prevent the target from acting, but are broken if they take direct damage.</p></li></ul>
-
