-  
-  <p>Hey everyone! We have one more build contest to run before Halloween festivities begin, and a new building mechanic for you to play with.</p><h4><strong>🔨Build Contest: Forge</strong></h4><p class="post-small">From magitech constructs to iron forges in deep dwarven mines.</p><ul><li><p>🗓️<strong>Due Date</strong>: Wednesday, September 18th, 2025 11:59 PM PDT</p><ul><li><p class="post-small">This event is also listed on the <a href="/calendar/">calendar</a>.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>✏️<strong>Prize Info</strong>: Can be found <a href="https://discord.com/channels/97121264988082176/1378477212805763112/1378477212805763112">here</a>.</p></li><li><p>🏆<strong>Special Prize</strong>: Entrants for the top 3 submissions earn <strong>+1 Charms slot</strong> and a free **<strong>Polaris</strong>** relic (see below!)</p></li></ul><h4><strong>💡Lights</strong></h4><p>A new Valor relic, <strong>Polaris</strong>, is available for purchase from Artificer Malachy for <em>1 Nether Star</em> + <em>4 Runes of Sparks</em>.</p><p>Inserting light-emitting blocks or Runes of Sparks into <strong>Polaris</strong> charges it. You can adjust its selected brightness, then &quot;place&quot; it to spawn an invisible light at that brightness, consuming an equivalent amount of charge. There is no cap to the charge, which also allows <strong>Polaris</strong> to act as an infinite sized stack of lights.</p><p>For example, torches give off 14 light, so inserting one adds 14 charge. You can use this to place 1 light of 14 brightness, or 2 lights of 7 brightness, and so on. Looking forward to seeing how you all use this to enhance your builds!</p><h2>🫶</h2>
