@@ -1,83 +0,0 @@
-
-  
-  <p class="post-emphasis">Greetings everyone! It’s time to formally announce our <em>Rush Weekends</em> and give a few fun general updates!</p><h4>Rush Weekends</h4><p>Rush Weekends are a new permanent feature of Silver Springs. They run every weekend for the full 24 hours of Saturday and Sunday, in Pacific time. The first will begin <strong>this Saturday, June 21st.</strong></p><p>Each rush activates a set of shared <strong>Core Bonuses</strong> to help you enjoy the weekend, as well as a random <strong>Wild Bonus</strong> from a list. Below are the <strong>Core Bonuses</strong> of each rush (every weekend!), as well as the <strong>Wild Bonus</strong> for the first rush this weekend - the <strong>River Rush</strong>!</p><p class="post-emphasis"><strong>✅Core Bonuses</strong></p><ul><li><p>+25% to earned Trial Points, mcMMO XP, and Boardwalk tickets, and to rune drop rates</p></li><li><p>The quest <strong>A Vexing Situation</strong> has only a 4-hour cooldown</p></li><li><p>mcMMO diminishing returns cap at 0.5x XP instead of 0.25x</p></li></ul><p class="post-emphasis"><strong>🐟Wild Bonus - River Rush!</strong></p><ul><li><p>It’s not SSS without rain and community fishing! During this rush, rain lasts longer and you’ll hook fish a bit quicker.</p></li></ul><h4><strong>General Updates</strong></h4><p><strong>🧍Armor stands</strong>:</p><ul><li><p>Updated the Armor Stand Customizer which is accessed by sneak right clicking armor stands:</p><ul><li><p>The smallness toggle has been replaced with +/- buttons to modify the armor stand&#x27;s scale between 0.2x and 2x.</p></li><li><p>Added a &quot;Swap Armor&quot; button to swap all armor the armor stand is wearing with your own.</p></li><li><p>Added a lower interface with editable slots to control equipment. This lets you put anything in their slots, including the hand slots for ones with arms.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>Added ‘/rotate info’, which allows punching an armor stand to view all of its current rotations.</p></li></ul><p><strong>📖Runecrafting balance</strong>, largely in preparation for the PvP tournament this weekend:</p><ul><li><p>Reduced the PvP damage of the <em>Avatar of Wardens</em> sonic blast from 5 ❤ to 1.5 ❤.</p></li><li><p>Reduced the damage of <em>Gatling</em>&#x27;s additional arrows by 50%.</p><ul><li><p class="post-small">This is harsh, but we believe justified. It too quickly outscales options like <em>Multishot</em>, and some of its power comes from the sheer projectile count, which increases reliability and proc rates, so it doesn&#x27;t need best-in-class damage within a few shots. It still scales into being the strongest DPS spread enchant.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>Halved the duration of <em>Adrenaline Rush</em>&#x27;s reduced speed and gravity in PvP.</p></li><li><p>Fixed <em>Ice Aspect</em> and <em>Plague Aspect</em> applying their effects even when the hit was blocked.</p></li></ul><p>✏️For those who were interested in the design behind the Arcanum expansion, a large post detailing the process is available here: <a href="/changelog-and-faq/designing-boundaries-of-the-arcanum/">Designing Boundaries of the Arcanum</a></p><p>✨Added the ‘/paragon’ command for viewing info about the existing Paragon items.</p><p>🪲Fixed mcMMO XP diminishing returns going down to 0.05x instead of our intended 0.25x. mcMMO was bugged and ignoring our config for this field.</p><p class="post-emphasis">Thanks, friends! Please leave feedback for any of this in ⁠#💌feedback-and-suggestions as usual. 🫶</p>
